EXPECTED: NO_DOS_EFFECT

REASON: Envoy 1.39.1 charges host header bytes against the per-stream limit before the discard path — assumption A1 is refuted

TARGET_IMAGE: envoyproxy/envoy:v1.39.1
TARGET_PORT: 443/tcp
CLIENT_TOOL: h2

DISPROOF_METHOD: assumption_refuted
DISPROOF_DETAIL: |
  Sent a HEADERS frame establishing a ~4000-byte host entry in the HPACK dynamic table,
  then sent CONTINUATION frames carrying ~1,000,000 indexed references against
  envoyproxy/envoy:v1.39.1. The stream was reset with PROTOCOL_ERROR once the per-stream
  header byte limit was reached; total copies were bounded well below 4 GB. Envoy process
  memory stayed within normal operating range. Static analysis of codec_impl.cc in
  v1.39.1 confirms that saveHeader() now charges all host bytes, including discarded
  ones, before the http2_discard_host_header return path. Fix introduced August 2026
  (CVE-2026-73550, patched in 1.39.1, 1.38.4, 1.37.6, 1.36.10).
DISPROOF_NOTES: Assumption A1 ("discarded host bytes not charged against limit") is
                refuted. The fix moves the per-stream byte accounting ahead of the
                discard branch in ServerConnectionImpl::onHeader(). The many-connection
                pivot is irrelevant: the attack is single-stream and each stream hits
                the per-stream byte limit independently.
